Governing text: SPEC §15 (`spec/15-dungeon-run.md:136`: "An artifact's map or fight effect counts once per level; a blessing's counts once.") and R2922001, whose "for each level" wording this copies. No new ruling.

## Steps

1. **Add the test first, so you see it fail.** In `crates/run/src/tests.rs`, insert this directly after the closing `}` of `r2922001_every_placeholder_curse_and_combat_artifact_has_a_fight_effect_its_text_states` (before the `// The mutation audit (#3513)` comment). `use super::*;` already brings in `RunEffect`, `RunPassiveKind` and `RUN_KEEP_MAX`.
   - Name it `placeholder_artifacts_with_a_map_effect_say_it_counts_for_each_level`. Give it no `r<n>` prefix, so R2922001's `proven_in` and `spec check` are untouched.
   - Do not rename or alter the R2922001 test. Its name says "curse and combat artifact", and its `proven_in` entry is the file `crates/run/src/tests.rs`.
   - Body:
     ```rust
     #[test]
     fn placeholder_artifacts_with_a_map_effect_say_it_counts_for_each_level() {
         // §15: an artifact's map effect counts once per level and a blessing's once, so each artifact's
         // text states its amount "for each level", as R2922001's Combat texts do, and no blessing's does.
         let content = content();
         let amount = |effect: RunEffect| match effect {
             RunEffect::KeepMore { n }
             | RunEffect::PackSize { n }
             | RunEffect::CoinsPerFight { n }
             | RunEffect::TicketsPerFight { n }
             | RunEffect::MaxHp { n } => n,
             RunEffect::Skip { coins } => coins,
             RunEffect::ShopDiscount { percent } => percent,
         };
         for passive in content
             .passives
             .iter()
             .filter(|p| p.kind == RunPassiveKind::Economic)
         {
             assert!(passive.effect.is_some(), "{} has a map effect", passive.id);
         }
         let (blessings, artifacts): (Vec<_>, Vec<_>) = content
             .passives
             .iter()
             .filter_map(|p| p.effect.map(|effect| (p, effect)))
             .partition(|(p, _)| p.kind == RunPassiveKind::Blessing);
         assert!(!artifacts.is_empty() && !blessings.is_empty());
         for (passive, effect) in artifacts {
             let (id, text) = (&passive.id, &passive.text);
             let n = amount(effect);
             assert!(text.contains(&n.to_string()), "{id}: {text:?} states {n}");
             assert!(text.contains("for each level"), "{id}: {text:?} says for each level");
             if matches!(effect, RunEffect::KeepMore { .. }) {
                 assert!(text.contains(&RUN_KEEP_MAX.to_string()), "{id}: {text:?} names its cap");
             }
         }
         for (passive, _) in blessings {
             assert!(
                 !passive.text.contains("for each level"),
                 "{}: {:?} counts once",
                 passive.id,
                 passive.text
             );
         }
     }
     ```
